# Chevill, Bane of Monsters {B}{G} 1/3 deathtouch: "At the beginning of your upkeep, if your opponents control no permanents with
# bounty counters on them, put a bounty counter on target creature or planeswalker an opponent controls" (CR 603.4, 122.1).
# Bot2 has two Memnites. Bot1's turn-3 upkeep puts a counter on the first (the intervening if is true: none has one). A Memnite
# without a counter then blocks and dies, which is no bounty death: Bot1 gains nothing. At turn 5's upkeep an opponent
# controls a bounty counter, so no second one goes on it (it stays at 1, and Chevill's own side never counted).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Chevill, Bane of Monsters
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite x2
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chevill, Bane of Monsters.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#1.Counters.Bounty = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Counters.Bounty = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Chevill, Bane of Monsters > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Memnite#2 > Chevill, Bane of Monsters)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Counters.Bounty = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
